    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties are delighted to present Hillside, a charming detached country residence occupying a mature and private site extending to approximately 0.3 acres in the sought-after Kilva area of East Cork.\r\nOriginally dating from circa 1900, this character-filled home has been thoughtfully upgraded and extended over the years to create a stylish and comfortable family residence. Extending to approximately 151.55 sq. m. (1,631 sq. ft.), the property offers flexible and well-proportioned accommodation ideally suited to modern family living, remote working and entertaining.\r\nSet behind mature boundaries and approached via a private driveway, Hillside enjoys a peaceful countryside setting while remaining just 5 minutes from Midleton town centre and the N25, offering easy access to Cork City, Waterford and beyond.\r\nThe location is particularly appealing, with East Ferry, Roches Point, Whitegate and Aghada all within easy reach. Residents can enjoy sailing, tennis, coastal walks, beaches and a host of outdoor pursuits, while Midleton provides an excellent range of schools, shopping, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities.\r\nA standout feature of the property is its versatility. With multiple reception areas, a dedicated home office, bar and entertaining space, detached garage, double carport and extensive outdoor areas, Hillside offers an exceptional balance of country living and modern practicality.\r\nAccommodation comprises: Entrance Hall, Living Room, Bar / Garden Room, Kitchen / Dining Room, Office / Bedroom 3, Ground Floor Bathroom, Two First Floor Bedrooms (Both En-Suite).\r\nGuide Price: €395, 000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\t \r\nEntrance Hall:\tWelcoming entrance hallway providing access to the principal reception rooms and staircase to first floor.\r\n\r\nLiving Room:\tA comfortable family reception room centred around a feature solid-fuel stove installed in 2019. \r\n\r\nBar / Garden Room:\tA versatile reception room featuring a built-in bar area and French doors opening directly onto the garden and patio, creating an ideal space for entertaining.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining Room:\tA spacious contemporary kitchen fitted with modern units, Belfast sink, integrated dishwasher, induction hob and tiled flooring. A step leads to the dining area which features timber flooring and French doors opening onto the courtyard area, allowing excellent natural light throughout the day.\r\n                                                \r\nOffice / Bedroom 3:\tCurrently utilised as a home office, this flexible room could equally serve as a ground-floor bedroom, playroom or additional reception room.\r\n\r\nGround Floor \r\nBathroom / Utility Room:\tComprising W.C., wash hand basin and utility area with washing machine and dryer. The room was previously fitted with a shower and retains the necessary plumbing should a purchaser wish to reinstate same.\r\nFirst Floor:\r\nMaster bedroom:                    A spacious double bedroom benefitting from extensive fitted storage and private en-suite accommodation.\r\n  \r\nEn-Suite:                                      Comprising W.C., wash hand basin and electric shower.\r\n          \r\nBedroom 2:                                 Generous double bedroom overlooking the surrounding countryside and benefitting from private en-suite accommodation.\r\n\r\nEn-Suite:\tComprising W.C., wash hand basin and electric shower.\r\n    \t\r\n\r\nOutside:    \tOccupying a mature site extending to approximately 0.3 acres, Hillside enjoys a private setting with beautifully maintained gardens and a variety of outdoor living spaces designed to maximise the property's tranquil countryside setting. A gravel driveway provides extensive parking and access to the detached garage, double carport, covered lean-to area and an additional attached garage / utility building adjoining the house. The detached garage benefits from electric roller doors, separate side access and its own upgraded fuse board, making it suitable for a variety of uses including workshop, storage or hobby space. The gardens have been thoughtfully arranged to create distinct outdoor areas, including a superb roof terrace overlooking the surrounding valley and countryside, accessed via a bridge from the upper garden. Additional features include built-in seating areas, a water feature, outdoor taps, mature planting and excellent privacy throughout."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tDetached country residence extending to approximately 151.55 sq. m. (1,631 sq. ft.)\r\n•\tBER B2 | BER No. 110754066\r\n•\tApprox. 0.3 acre mature site\r\n•\tFibre-to-the-home broadband\r\n•\tContemporary kitchen with Belfast sink, integrated dishwasher and induction hob\r\n•\tTwo spacious first-floor bedrooms, both with en-suite facilities\r\n•\tDedicated home office / optional third bedroom\r\n•\tBar and entertaining room\r\n•\tDetached garage with electric roller door and separate fuse board\r\n•\tAdditional attached garage / utility room\r\n•\tDouble carport and covered lean-to\r\n•\tRoof terrace with elevated countryside and valley views\r\n•\tBuilt-in outdoor seating areas\r\n•\tWater feature within the landscaped gardens\r\n•\tExtensive private parking\r\n•\t5 minutes from Midleton Town Centre\r\n•\tEasy access to East Ferry, Whitegate, Aghada and Roches Point"
